   "source": [
    "# Search-Guided Evolutionary Optimization for Graph Pathfinding\n",
    "\n",
    ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5c18043c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Problem statement and research questions\n",
    "\n",
    "Path planning requires a route from a start node to a goal while balancing feasibility, path length, traversal cost, and search effort. Classical methods provide different guarantees and resource trade-offs. Evolutionary methods can support flexible objectives, but stochastic initialization can affect reliability.\n",
    "\n",
    "This project asks:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. How do uninformed, cost-based, and heuristic searches compare on unit-cost and weighted obstacle grids?\n",
    "2. Does A* seeding improve Genetic Algorithm convergence, solution quality, success rate, or stability?\n",
    "3. How do grid size and obstacle density affect search effort and evolutionary runtime?\n",
    "\n",
    "The original HW01 and HW02 notebooks are retained as legacy coursework. Their actual contents are documented in the repository README and are not misrepresented as graph-search implementations."
   ]
  },
